                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            The energy column is simple arithmetic: amp-hours times the 12.8V nominal voltage of a LiFePO4 battery. It shows why capacity, not brand, is the first decision. Two budget 100Ah batteries store the same energy as one 206Ah battery and about three-quarters of a 270Ah battery. Which configuration suits you depends on space, weight, budget and how much current your inverter needs, all of which are covered below.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you do not have a built-in RV electrical system and just want portable power for a campsite, a dedicated lithium battery may not be the right purchase. A <a href="/best-portable-power-station/">portable power station</a> packages a LiFePO4 battery, inverter and charger together. The section on portable lithium battery packs explains when that is the better route.
          </p>
        </div>

