          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most RV owners, a 12V 100Ah LiFePO4 battery is the right starting point: the Battle Born 100Ah if you want the strongest support, the LiTime 12V 100Ah if you would rather spend the savings on a second battery. Cold-weather campers should buy self-heating, and full-timers should look at larger batteries like the SOK 206Ah or Battle Born 270Ah GC3.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
